title: Konni Operation Conflict Compass OneDriveUpdateScheduler Scheduled Task
id: 84ad05ae-c591-4224-a7b5-f2b24ce9a427
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects command lines creating the OneDriveUpdateScheduler scheduled task,
    the persistence mechanism of the Konni (TA406/Opal Sleet) Operation
    Conflict Compass campaign against Ukraine-focused entities: a LNK lure
    disguised as a PDF downloads a VBScript that registers the task to launch
    the VelvetCake PowerShell payload every minute (SOCRadar, September 2026).
references:
    - https://cyberpress.org/konni-targets-ukraine-with-velvetcake/
    - https://gbhackers.com/velvetcake-powershell-malware/
    - https://malware.news/t/konni-cv-olesiatsvientukh-socialresearcher-sociologist-qualitativelnk/125920#post_1
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/09/28
tags:
    - attack.t1053
    - attack.t1086
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_schtasks:
        Image|endswith: '\schtasks.exe'
        CommandLine|contains: 'OneDriveUpdateScheduler'
    selection_shell:
        Image|endswith:
            - '\powershell.exe'
            - '\pwsh.exe'
            - '\cmd.exe'
        CommandLine|contains: 'OneDriveUpdateScheduler'
    condition: selection_schtasks or selection_shell
falsepositives:
    - Security research or red-team tooling reproducing the published campaign artifacts
    - A legitimate updater task coincidentally named OneDriveUpdateScheduler (unlikely)
level: high
